---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION}>
	<h1>About Me</h1>
	<p>
		Hello! I'm <strong>Marlon Brandão de Sousa</strong>, a software engineer based in Curitiba,
		Brazil. I have worked in technology since 2003, and for much of that time on the systems that
		move people's money: internet banking, international remittances, and cross-border payments.
	</p>
	<p>
		I am also a blind developer, a conference speaker, and a digital accessibility advocate. Those
		two halves are not separate careers. Building financial software that people trust — and that
		everyone can actually use — is the same problem approached from two directions, and it is the
		work I care most about.
	</p>

	<h2>Professional Experience</h2>
	<ul>
		<!-- Dates omitted below: LinkedIn masks them for logged-out visitors.
		     Add them from the Positions export when convenient. -->
		<li>
			<strong>EBANX — Software Engineering:</strong> Engineering at one of Latin America's largest
			fintechs, building the cross-border payments infrastructure that global merchants use to sell
			into the region. I also help run the
			<strong>EBANX Software Engineering Showcase</strong>, our public technical meetup in Curitiba,
			where we talk openly about how we build software that has to be both fast and trustworthy.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Remessa Online — Software Engineer Specialist:</strong> International money transfers.
			Engineering on the platform that moves funds across borders for individuals and businesses.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Itaú Unibanco — Internet Banking Platform:</strong> Development and evolution of the
			framework behind the internet banking of Brazil's largest private bank, along with maintenance
			of the internet banking core system and the design of interoperability layers between systems.
			I also advised mobile and internet banking front-end teams on accessibility.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Earlier — Communications &amp; Consulting:</strong> Roles across software development,
			quality assurance, process control, and systems analysis at large Brazilian companies, starting
			in 2003.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Speaking &amp; Community</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Founder &amp; Editor-in-Chief — BlindTec:</strong> I created and lead
			<a href="https://www.blindtec.com.br" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BlindTec</a>,
			Brazil's leading portal and podcast for assistive technology, publishing technical articles,
			tutorials, and interviews on screen readers, software accessibility, and tech careers.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Track Coordinator &amp; Speaker — The Developer's Conference (TDC):</strong> Coordinator
			of the Accessibility track at TDC São Paulo, and a speaker at TDC Porto Alegre and DevDay Belo
			Horizonte on accessibility, entrepreneurship, and the craft of programming.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Writing &amp; Podcasts:</strong> Most recently on AI agents delivering real business
			value in production at EBANX, past the hype. Previously interviewed on
			<em>podProgramar</em>, one of Brazil's best-known programming podcasts.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>EasyWay — second place, FIAP StartupOne:</strong> With a designer and two other
			engineers, I built the prototype of an indoor location system to help people find their way
			through complex venues such as expo centres, shopping malls, and stadiums.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Areas of Interest</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Payments &amp; Financial Systems:</strong> Correctness, reliability, and trust in
			systems where being wrong costs somebody real money.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Rust Development:</strong> My language of choice. I am interested in the case that
			Rust is not only for systems work — that you can write command line tools, services, and
			desktop applications in it at a high level of abstraction and still get the performance,
			the deployment story, and the safety guarantees for free.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Assistive Technology &amp; Screen Readers:</strong> Extending NVDA, screen reader
			ergonomics, and cross-platform accessibility across Windows, Linux, and mobile.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>AI-Driven Agent Automation:</strong> Model Context Protocol servers such as
			<code>screen-readers-mcp</code>, which let AI agents drive screen readers to run automated
			functional tests — bringing real test coverage to software that has historically been checked
			by hand, if at all.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Quality Engineering:</strong> Building testable architectures with accessibility
			designed in from day one rather than retrofitted before an audit.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Education</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Postgraduate MBA in Mobile &amp; Game Development:</strong> FIAP</li>
		<li><strong>B.S. in IT Management:</strong> Unisul</li>
		<li><strong>Technical Diploma in Data Processing:</strong> Etec Lauro Gomes</li>
	</ul>

